## Noise: what to skip in the log context

The log context above contains many non‑porcelain lines. Skip all lines matching any category below — they are never valid path sources:

**Orchestrator lifecycle:** phase transitions, `>>> Phase …`, `=== … Orchestrator ===`, `=== CI Debug Round … ===`, module progress/status tables, heartbeats, wave banners, progress summaries (`Total: … done / … failed`), `ERROR:` lines about merge conflicts or module failures, `Rebase PAUSED`, `L1 agent could not resolve`, `Applying L2 …`, `Both repos have clean …`, `Sent message to agent session:`, `DEBUG SUPERVISOR`, `DEBUG DISPATCHED`, `Session … no longer exists on disk`, `No code changes from debug agents`, `Nothing to commit`, `Build state:`, `Build created:`, `Build triggered:`, `Downloaded log:`, `Triage report:`, finalization/email lines.

**CI/Buildkite pipeline:** `Running [N/M]:`, `PASSED:`, `FAILED:`, `SKIP`, `RETRY`, `RETRY PASSED:`, `IGNORE (nightly baseline):`, `Command:` lines, `pytest` invocations, `GPU lock`, `rc=`, `::error`, `file:` references, `RETRY ':step name'`, `Retry triggered (new job ...)`.

**Git non-porcelain:** commit headers `[branch hash] …`, diff stat (`N files changed`), `create mode`/`delete mode`, push output (`To https://`, `HEAD -> …`), `Auto-merging` lines, `Automatic merge failed`.

**Log framing:** `[2026-…]` timestamps, `INFO`/`WARNING`/`DEBUG`/`ERROR` log-level prefixes, `/rebase/…` absolute paths.

**Environment/build:** `SSH fetch failed`, `wheel URL`, `Wheel URL already matches`, `API drift`, `Upstream import`, `Dockerfile.ci updated`, `vLLM already at target commit`, `Found wheel at commit:`, `Error: Input must be provided either through stdin or as a prompt argument`, lines with `bare=`/`worktree=`, `slug=`, wheel/uv/HTTP/SSH/ROCm tokens, diffstat (`++++`/`----`), `diff --git`, `site-packages/`, `.cache/uv/`.

**Agent/watchdog:** `[watchdog]` verdicts, `Agent verdict:`, `Potential error detected, asking agent to review:`, `Using level-* agent model:`.

**Refinement/summary:** `POST_RUN_REFINEMENT`, `Sending failure notification`, `send_failure_notification:`, `Running post-run self-refinement`, agent‑generated summary prose, `Path sync report`, `Commit assignment report`, post‑refinement markdown headers and bullet lists, `FINAL_SUMMARY.md`.

**Pre-commit:** hook names with `...Passed`/`...Skipped`, `- hook id:`, `Fixing …`, ruff/format banners.

**Other:** module‑debug session lines, `Skipping <module>` in resume mode.

**Path traps:** Paths next to `CONFLICT`, `Merge conflicts detected in:`, `Automatic merge failed`, `Auto-staging resolved conflict file`, or `L1 agent could not resolve` — ignore unless the **same** path also appears as an `XY`/`??` line in a porcelain block below.

**Aggregate failure skepticism:** If the log shows all modules failing simultaneously (e.g. `(0/6)` plateau then `(6/6)`), paths from those modules are likely rebase artifacts, not intentional work. Prefer **discard**.

